Question: <memory_context>
[2026-09-22 00:00:00] Subquery 1: What are the known cases of teens dying in vehicular accidents between 2008 and 2016 where it is reported that their tissues were donated and the recipients included another child?

Predicted Answer: Explanation: The strongest match is the case of AJ Perez. He was an 18-year-old Filipino actor who died on April 17, 2011, when the van he was riding in was sideswiped by a bus in Moncada, Tarlac [62478][31584]. His corneas were donated: one cornea went to John Daniel delos Santos, who was 8 years old at the time of the transplant, and the other went to 28-year-old Lawrence Villanueva [58107][62478][13127]. Since corneas are ocular tissue, this meets the “tissues donated” criterion and the recipient was clearly another child. Other teen car-accident donors in the retrieved records—such as Jordan Aucoin, Abby Cecena, Joshua Florence, Rachel Givens, and Sydnee—were reported as organ/tissue donors, but the retrieved accounts do not state that any of their recipients were children [60316][88982]. Another potential case, Kathryn Gardia, was a teen in a crash whose tissue was procured, but her death occurred in 2007, outside the requested range, and no recipient age was reported [63157]. Therefore, based on the available evidence, AJ Perez is the only case that fully satisfies all the stated criteria.

Exact Answer: AJ Perez (Antonello Joseph Sarte Perez), an 18-year-old who died in a vehicular accident on April 17, 2011; his donated corneas included one transplanted to 8-year-old John Daniel delos Santos. Based on the retrieved evidence, this is the only fully confirmed case meeting all stated criteria; no other confirmed case was found in the available documents.

